            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0521" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/545: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-02T17:00:00-05:00">December 2, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>399. I desire to express my high appreciation of the promptness and complete
                    success with which you have carried out at each step my instructions in
                    connection with the action which I am taking in regard to the Russo-Chinese
                    situation.</p>
                <p>You may also express to the Minister for Foreign Affairs my appreciation of his
                    prompt and cordial cooperation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
